00:39:05.780 --> 00:39:09.020
I wanted to mention two more
things before we were done.

00:39:09.020 --> 00:39:12.380
One of them is that we actually
do-- and this is not a product

00:39:12.380 --> 00:39:15.980
announcement session,
but we actually

00:39:15.980 --> 00:39:18.370
have announced a couple
of products today.

00:39:18.370 --> 00:39:20.360
I mentioned hybrid
earlier for Apigee.

00:39:20.360 --> 00:39:23.600
Hybrid is a way that you
can take the API gateway

00:39:23.600 --> 00:39:26.390
part of Apigee, which is
what Keith was just demoing,

00:39:26.390 --> 00:39:29.600
and run that anywhere you want,
including your own data center

00:39:29.600 --> 00:39:32.870
while the rest of Apigee such
as the API analytics, the API

00:39:32.870 --> 00:39:34.550
product management,
and all those kinds

00:39:34.550 --> 00:39:36.980
of things including some
of the user interface

00:39:36.980 --> 00:39:38.275
runs in Google's Cloud.

00:39:38.275 --> 00:39:40.400
This is something our
customers have been asking us

00:39:40.400 --> 00:39:43.183
for a long time because
many, many customers

00:39:43.183 --> 00:39:44.600
even if they are
completely bought

00:39:44.600 --> 00:39:46.130
into cloud computing
many of them

00:39:46.130 --> 00:39:49.460
still have, and may have
for a long time to come,

00:39:49.460 --> 00:39:51.470
stuff that runs in
their own data centers

00:39:51.470 --> 00:39:53.720
or even in other clouds
or in private clouds.

00:39:53.720 --> 00:39:55.760
So Apigee hybrid gives
you a way to do this.

00:39:55.760 --> 00:39:57.890
That is in beta starting today.

00:39:57.890 --> 00:40:00.390
We also have something called
API security reporting,

00:40:00.390 --> 00:40:03.020
which is based on some of the
analytics that Keith showed.

00:40:03.020 --> 00:40:04.820
It gives you a little
bit more details

00:40:04.820 --> 00:40:07.280
about how your API
traffic is behaving

00:40:07.280 --> 00:40:10.580
and it alerts you to things
like anomalous API traffic.

00:40:10.580 --> 00:40:13.760
Or even mistakes you might have
made like not configuring TLS

00:40:13.760 --> 00:40:15.770
properly for your APIs.

00:40:15.770 --> 00:40:18.050
And finally, some of the
policies that Keith showed in

00:40:18.050 --> 00:40:20.240
that policy editor
are actually things

00:40:20.240 --> 00:40:22.670
that you can extend
yourself using a capability

00:40:22.670 --> 00:40:24.360
called Apigee extensions.

00:40:24.360 --> 00:40:27.200
There are pre-built extensions
for many popular integration

00:40:27.200 --> 00:40:31.100
technologies like SAP, like
many of the Google Cloud APIs.

00:40:31.100 --> 00:40:34.340
And yes, also many of the
Amazon APIs because many of you

00:40:34.340 --> 00:40:36.560
use Amazon APIs as well.

00:40:36.560 --> 00:40:39.020
Apigee extensions
is fully GA now

00:40:39.020 --> 00:40:42.770
it's been part of the Apigee
product for a little while.

